! Example initial-conditions namelist for INITIAL_CONDITIONS::READ_IC_NAMELIST
! (src/core/initial_conditions.f90). Not yet read by any driver -- see
! ROADMAP.md programming task 4 for status; this file documents the
! format and can be copied/edited once a driver wires in an optional
! namelist-path CLI argument.
!
! &IC_SELECT names the list of ACTIVE tags (composable by design,
! 2026-08-29: every active tag's contribution accumulates into the same
! Phi/Psi, so e.g. a future force-free base plus a Bessel-Riccati
! perturbation could both be listed here at once). READ_IC_NAMELIST then
! reads whichever model-specific group(s) those tags name. Only
! 'bessel_riccati' exists so far, so this example lists just the one.
&IC_SELECT
  N_TAGS = 1
  TAGS   = 'bessel_riccati'
/

! Each mode contributes f_n(x) = A*x*j_n(x) + B*x*y_n(x), x = X_SCALE*r,
! to either PHI or PSI at spherical-harmonic degree/order (L,M). Modes
! sharing the same (FIELD,L,M) accumulate (superpose), so a single
! (l,m) can carry a multi-n radial spectrum by repeating it across
! several array entries. j_n/y_n are evaluated by SPHERICAL_BESSEL --
! stable to n=20 (src/core/spherical_bessel.f90).
!
! This example reproduces this project's own long-standing ad hoc seed
! IC (Phi(l=1,m=0)=sin(pi*(r-R_min)/(R_max-R_min)), Psi=0) is NOT what's
! below -- that profile isn't a Riccati-Bessel combination. Below is
! instead a simple single-mode illustration: at n=0, x*j_0(x)=sin(x), so
! this reduces to Phi(l=1,m=0,r) = sin(r) with X_SCALE=1 (a plain
! amplitude-1, A-branch-only, n=0 mode).
&BESSEL_RICCATI_MODES
  N_MODES      = 1
  MODE_FIELD   = 'phi'
  MODE_L       = 1
  MODE_M       = 0
  MODE_N       = 0
  MODE_X_SCALE = 1.0
  MODE_A       = 1.0
  MODE_B       = 0.0
/
